            <ArticleTitle>Discovery and optimization of orally active cyclohexane-based prolylcarboxypeptidase (PrCP) inhibitors.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>6228-33</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.bmcl.2013.09.094</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0960-894X(13)01180-3</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The synthesis, SAR, binding affinities and pharmacokinetic profiles are described for a series of cyclohexane-based prolylcarboxypeptidase (PrCP) inhibitors discovered by high throughput screening. Compounds show high levels of ex vivo target engagement in mouse plasma 20 h post oral dose.</AbstractText>
